# Fenoa's service presets for the desktop stage. Every unit images/fenoa/Containerfile enables in
# the desktop stage needs a line here, for the reason given in 50-fenoa.preset: a first boot runs a
# full preset pass, and 99-default-disable.preset disables whatever no preset lists.

# The login screen (D5). Fedora's 85-display-manager.preset enables gdm, sddm and the like but not
# greetd, so without this line the first boot would disable greetd and come up with no greeter.
enable greetd.service

# D5's `systemctl set-default graphical.target` is the symlink /etc/systemd/system/default.target.
# graphical.target has no [Install] section, so a full preset pass "disables" it by deleting that
# link, and the default falls back to the base image's /usr/lib/systemd/system/default.target
# (graphical.target today). This line keeps the image's own choice in place.
enable graphical.target
